{"summary": "The proposal focuses on aesthetic 'immersion' but ignores critical performance and state failures in the current implementation, specifically regarding image loading and navigation.",
"verdict": "REVISE",
"items": [{"issue": "Stale image events and race conditions in ArtBackdrop transition logic.", "evidence": "src/art/ArtBackdrop.tsx: useEffect triggers 'settle' 2400ms after state.ready, regardless of whether the artwork has changed in the interim.", "change": "Bind the settle timer to the specific artwork ID and ensure the cleanup function cancels pending transitions when the artwork prop changes.", "check": "Verify that rapid artwork switching does not result in the wrong image being set as the base layer."}, {"issue": "Performance degradation and memory leaks from unmanaged image instances.", "evidence": "src/art/ArtBackdrop.tsx: Maps over [state.base, state.incoming] creating multiple ArtScene components without a strategy to unload previous assets.", "change": "Implement a cache-clearing mechanism or explicit nullification of the 'base' image once the 'incoming' image has fully settled.", "check": "Monitor memory usage during long 'Play collection' sessions to ensure DOM nodes and image buffers are released."}, {"issue": "Poor rapid navigation accessibility and UX in ArtViewer.", "evidence": "src/art/ArtViewer.tsx: move() resets elapsed.current to 0, but the 250ms setInterval continues to run, potentially causing jumpy transitions during manual skipping.", "change": "Synchronize the auto-advance timer with manual navigation to prevent immediate double-skips and ensure the 'loaded' state is verified before triggering the next transition.", "check": "Confirm that clicking 'Next' rapidly does not trigger the auto-advance logic prematurely."}]}
